# Development happens on Windows; everything runs on Linux.
#
# A shell script checked out with CRLF fails on the target with a baffling
# error -- `bash: /root/x.sh: cannot execute: required file not found`, or
# `$'\r': command not found` -- which looks like a missing interpreter rather
# than a line-ending problem. Force LF on everything that Linux executes or
# parses.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.toml text eol=lf
*.ini text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.mako text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
.env.example text eol=lf

*.tgz binary
*.png binary
*.zst binary
